-04T13:01:31Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T22:25:29Z","closed_at":"2026-09-11T22:25:29Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.6.dev.custom_build [06827c91c]\n- Reproducible in v4.5.1.rc.custom_build [c834443ef]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.rc (c834443ef) - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 19 Sep 2025 16:09:36 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7900 XT (RADV NAVI31) - AMD Ryzen 9 7900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 30.49 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nParagraph spacing for docs in the in-editor help is inconsistent between official Godot classes and custom classes using doc comments. More specifically, custom classes have much less spacing between paragraphs.\n\n`Node._enter_tree()`:\n<img width=\"1094\" height=\"159\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bc3bbcbc-f3b8-43be-b530-099be66c5dbd\" />\n\nCustom class copying `Node._enter_tree()`:\n<img width=\"1094\" height=\"138\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b6a80555-ba4f-4f23-8fab-62fe32b82ade\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a custom class, copy a property/method description from an official class (e.g. `Node`).\n- Open the documentation for the official class.\n- Open the documentation for your custom class and compare the results.\n\nFor reference, here's the `Node._enter_tree()` method description, copied directly from the XML file (leading tabs removed):\n```\nCalled when the node enters the [SceneTree] (e.g. upon instantiating, scene changing, or after calling [method add_child] in a script). If the node has children, its [method _enter_tree] callback will be called first, and then that of the children.\nCorresponds to the [constant NOTIFICATION_ENTER_TREE] notification in [method Object._notification].\n```\nAnd the GDScript doc comments used to copy it:\n```gdscript\n## Called when the node enters the [SceneTree] (e.g. upon instantiating, scene changing,\n## or after calling [method add_child] in a script). If the node has children,\n## its [method _enter_tree] callback will be called first, and then that of the children.[br]\n## Corresponds to the [constant NOTIFICATION_ENTER_TREE] notification in\n## [method Object._notification].\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A (you can copy the sample above)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111252/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}